SUMMARY:Whiteville Teen Science Cafe: Wildlife Storytelling
DESCRIPTION:Ben Zino started his YouTube channel\, The Wild Report\, when he was 15 years old and has grown his audience to more than 80\,000 subscribers. Come find out how Ben uses his love for wildlife\, his dedication for conservation\, and his passion for storytelling to connect viewers with local wildlife. \nJoin us for our December Cafe as Ben shares his journey from a kid that loves reptiles and amphibians to the Curator of Visitor Services at the NC Museum of Natural Sciences at Whiteville and the Creative Director of The Wild Report. \nABOUT THE SPEAKER \nThis program is led by conservation biologist and science communicator Ben Zino. An NC State graduate with a masters degree in Conservation Biology\, Ben has turned his passion for sharing the natural world with others into a career as both a museum educator and wildlife content creator. \nFor questions about this event\, contact the museum at 910-788-5100 or whiteville@naturalsciences.org.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/whiteville-teen-science-cafe-wildlife-storytelling/
LOCATION:Whiteville\, 415 South Madison Street\, Whiteville\, NC\, 28472\, United States
CATEGORIES:Science Cafes,Teens
